$ zenctl retire --help
Retire a key with a tombstone — an authoritative delete (RFC 04 §1.2), riding a declared publisher like `pub` (P7).

State keys retire freely (retirement is the class's own semantics); anything else is an operator cleanup (v1.12) and needs --i-know. Wildcards are refused outright.

Usage: zenctl retire [OPTIONS] <KEY>

Arguments:
  <KEY>
          Full wire key to retire (concrete — wildcards are refused)

Options:
      --qos <QOS>
          QoS profile for the tombstone (RFC 04 §3). A retirement is the final state transition, so it defaults to the reliable profile
          
          [default: transition]

      --i-know
          Retire a key that is not state-shaped — the RFC 04 §1.2 (v1.12) operator act. The refusal you are overriding names its reason

